{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And the people feared HaShem</b> — meaning, the fear of exaltedness; but fear of punishment they had already possessed previously in Egypt. Yet according to what we demonstrated in parashat (Exodus 12:43) ״זֹאת חֻקַּת הַפָּסַח״ — that they did not accept upon themselves the commandments of the King — if so, not even fear of punishment did they possess until they saw the great hand, ״וַיִּירְאוּ״ etc., and in any case the verse is speaking of the fear of exaltedness, as indicated by its saying ״וַיַּרְא יִשְׂרָאֵל אֶת הַיָּד הַגְּדוֹלָה וַיִּירְאוּ״ etc. And its saying <b>and they believed</b> — for this is the fulfillment of faith within them."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:28:12.232012761Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}